<title>MEXICO: Bacardi Mexico arm says '96 sales up 40 pct on '95.</title>
<headline>Bacardi Mexico arm says '96 sales up 40 pct on '95.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcoholic beverages maker Bacardi expects sales revenues in 1996 to be substantially above 1995 figures, the company's Mexican boss said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Last year was a bad one. In 1996, we will close 40 percent up in monetary terms,&quot; said Isaac Chertorivski, chairman of the board at Bacardi, in reply to questions from journalists.</p>
<p>Chertorivski said that Bacardi held a 30 percent share of the Mexican wines and spirits market.</p>
<p>-- Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397</p>
</text>
